// QA-authored golden-vector test for weapi / eapi.
//
// The expected values below were computed by QA independently, in
// `qa-verify/golden.js` (Node.js `crypto`), directly from the Swift source
// `harken/Sources/Harken/Core/API/NeteaseCrypto.swift`:
//   weapi = AES-128-CBC(presetKey "0CoJUm6Qyw8W8jud", IV "0102030405060708")
//           -> base64 -> AES-128-CBC("harken2026abcDEF", same IV) -> base64
//           （注："harken2026abcDEF" 是客户端自选的 weapi secretKey（与预计算 RSA
//             encSecKey 配对）；可随品牌改名，但必须同步重算 encSecKey）
//   eapi  = AES-128-ECB("e82ckenh8dichen8") over
//           "nobody{apiPath}use{text}md5forencrypt" md5 digest,
//           emitted as UPPERCASE hex
//
// Payloads are supplied as raw bytes (byteArrayOf) so that no JSON
// serialisation difference can mask a cipher mismatch. The matrix covers
// ASCII, Chinese, an escape-heavy body, a 4 KB body, a single byte, an empty
// object and a rare-CJK plane-2 character.
//
// This file is deliberately NOT a copy of the engineer's
// `NeteaseCryptoTest` + `weapi-golden.json`: a test that only replays the
// implementation's own fixtures cannot detect a mis-transcription of the
// shared constants.

package com.rc.harken.net.crypto

import org.junit.Assert.assertEquals
import org.junit.Assert.assertTrue
import org.junit.Test

